  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a Black man in a suit laughing broadly while overlaid text reads, 'see... i told you cyril. the majority in sa do not mind us stealing from them..'. The text implies a racially charged accusation that South Africans are complicit in or tolerant of theft by outsiders, using a dehumanizing and economically reductive stereotype. This frames Black South Africans as passive recipients of exploitation, reinforcing harmful narratives of racial hierarchy and economic victimhood. The meme's intent is to provoke division and hostility by weaponizing racialized economic grievances, targeting Black South Africans as a group through the use of derogatory and false assumptions about their attitudes toward theft and economic injustice. The visual of the laughing man juxtaposed with the text amplifies the message of contempt and superiority, making it a hateful meme that attacks a specific racial group based on protected characteristics.",
